{
  "title": "Recipe text search rechecks every old version, making common-word searches slow",
  "description": "The trigram search indexes from migration 2026-04-16-000000-0000_unaccent_search are on recipe_versions, so they cover every historical version, not just each recipe's current one. \
For a common word, the bitmap index scans in GET /api/recipes match thousands of rows (most of them old versions), and each one is rechecked with f_unaccent() over the full instructions and ingredients::text before the join to recipes.current_version_id throws it away. \
With scripts/sqlite-pilot-bench.py at 5k recipes x 3 versions, EXPLAIN ANALYZE shows about 300 ms server-side for 'chicken', and end-to-end search took about 0.5 s (doc/sqlite-pilot-analysis.md). \
Fix options: partial or expression indexes limited to current versions (for example an is_current flag maintained on version writes), or a separate search table keyed by recipe holding only the current text. \
Add a regression check that EXPLAIN for a common token doesn't recheck non-current versions. \
Moot if the SQLite cutover in blocked-database-generic-sqlite-step2 lands first, since that plan indexes current versions only.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
